Description:

A calendar sharee without the mayWriteAll or mayWriteOwn right can no longer
change an event's sequence number, whether through JMAP CalendarEvent/set or
a CalDAV PUT.  Previously the per-property permission check let any sharee
who held mayRSVP (or the per-event mayInviteSelf/mayInviteOthers grants) set
SEQUENCE to any value, even though every other organizer-controlled property
was refused.

CalendarEvent/set no longer bumps SEQUENCE on behalf of such a sharee when they
RSVP or add an invitee: the organizer's revision counter is left to the
organizer and other writers with full rights.


